course: dictionary
lesson: 10757
title: Urine: the body's liquid waste
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your body makes waste, and it must get rid of it. Urine is the yellow liquid waste your body makes and passes out when you go to the toilet. The kidneys clean your blood and make urine, which is stored in the bladder until you go.
explain: Urine is an uncountable noun, so we say some urine, never two urines. Children in Britain often use the everyday word «wee» for it, and it means the same thing. Doctors test urine samples to learn about your health.
explain: We lose water every day in sweat, breath and urine. «We lose water every day in sweat, breath and urine, so we must drink it every day.» Pale yellow urine usually means you drink enough water, but dark urine can mean you need more.
fact: Urine is liquid waste that the body makes.
fact: The kidneys clean the blood and make urine.
fact: Urine is stored in the bladder until you go to the toilet.
fact: «Wee» is the British everyday word for urine or to urinate.
fact: Birds make no runny urine: their waste comes out as a white paste, together with dark poo.
exercise: «Urine is the yellow liquid waste your body makes and passes out.» What is urine? | Blood from the heart | *Liquid waste made by the body | Air breathed out | A kind of food
exercise: Which part of the body cleans the blood and makes urine? | *Kidneys | Stomach | Heart | Lungs
exercise: «We lose water every day in sweat, breath and urine.» Name one way the body loses water. | Sleeping | *Sweat | Eating bread | Growing taller
test: Dark urine can mean what? | You have eaten too many sweets | You have grown a lot this year | You need more sleep | *You need to drink more water
test: Where is urine stored until you go to the toilet? | The stomach | *The bladder | The ears | The brain
exam: Which is the correct way to write it, since urine is uncountable? | *Some urine | Two urines | Three urines | Many urines
